    description: "A source-backed route from chapter 77 to connected guidance on additional amounts, payments, income and capital. Authored navigation awaiting specialist review."
    body: |
      # Find the connected guidance

      This project-authored navigation aid follows the signposts in chapter 77, paragraph 77003, across PDF pages 3 and 4. Those signposts identify where another topic is discussed. They do not establish a claimant's entitlement or show that every condition has been captured.

      | Research topic | Chapter indicated in paragraph 77003 |
      | --- | --- |
      | Additional amounts and special groups | 78 |
      | Payment questions | 79 |
      | Transitional provisions | 80 |
      | Assessed income periods | 83 |
      | Capital and deemed weekly income from capital | 84 |
      | Income other than earnings | 85 |
      | Earnings | 86 |

      Chapter 80 is retained in the source inventory and the scope note because it contains transitional provisions. It is not merged into the default seven-chapter search corpus. Chapters 81 and 82 are explicitly spare.

      Paragraph 77003 also points outside this two-volume attachment snapshot, including other Decision makers' guide chapters and Advice for decision making. External memos and cited legislation require separate acquisition and verification before the graph can claim to capture those dependencies.

      ## Follow an evidence route

      1. Open the relevant chapter and source page.
      2. Keep definitions, exceptions, dates, examples and footnotes together.
      3. Follow any referenced memo, legislation or other chapter on the official source.
      4. Record which dependencies remain unverified before making a domain claim.

      The graph edges from this research aid to chapters are authored navigational references. They are not formal legal dependencies or a transcription of every cross-reference in the corpus.

